So they spoke, and shook it the Gerenian horseman Nestor,
and out leapt a lot from the helmet, the very one they themselves wished for,
Ajax’s;

for no one by force, willing, will drive me, unwilling,
nor by skill either, since not even me, so ignorant,
I expect, was born and reared in Salamis.”

And him the Argives rejoiced, looking at him,
but upon the Trojans a fearsome trembling crept, upon the limbs of each,
and for Hector himself the heart in his chest pounded;

second, in turn,
Zeus-sprung Ajax sent forth his long-shadowed spear,
and hit the son of Priam on the shield, equal on every side;

But not even so did Hector of the glancing helmet leave off from battle,
but drawing back he took a stone in his stout hand,
lying on the plain, black and rough and great;

And now indeed with swords at close quarters they would have been striking each other,
if the heralds, messengers of Zeus and also of men,
had not come, one of the Trojans, the other of the bronze-shirted Achaeans,
Talthybius and Idaeus, the two prudent;
